        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hindmarsh Stadium, Adelaide, South Australia, Semaphore Park\n- Organizations: Coopers Brewery, Adelaide United FC\n- Products: Coopers Stadium\n- Places: Fort Glanville Conservation Park\n\nFacts:\n- Hindmarsh Stadium is a multi-purpose stadium located in Adelaide, South Australia.\n- Hindmarsh Stadium is currently known as Coopers Stadium because of sponsorship from the Adelaide-based Coopers Brewery.\n- In the 2013 financial year, Coopers Brewery sold 69.7 million litres of beer.\n- Adelaide United FC uses Hindmarsh Stadium as its home ground.\n- Fort Glanville Conservation Park is a protected area in Semaphore Park, a seaside suburb of Adelaide, South Australia.\n- Fort Glanville Conservation Park includes a functional 19th-century fort listed on the South Australian Heritage Register and some adjoining land.",
